  "description": "<p>I have encountered a problem where Fedora fails to start if MySQL is not fully ready at the time of Fedora startup. This is a problem during bootstrapping of my server, since even if I create a dependency between Fedora and MySQL, systemd will sometimes attempt to start Fedora before MySQL is ready to receive connections.</p>\n\n<p>This was discussed on the August 17, 2023 dev call. Consensus was that it would make sense for Fedora to introduce a “wait-and-retry” loop around database initialization, so that it doesn’t immediately fail when a dependency is offline. Ideally, the wait duration and retry limit could be configurable via Java properties so that the behavior could be customized and/or disabled.</p>",
